																		The innate nature of things.
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/meitwouldseem" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7058969); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7058969&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606683206" alt="MeitWouldSeem" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7058969)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/meitwouldseem" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7058969); return false;" >MeitWouldSeem</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606518584 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">27 Nov 2020 23:09</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4829726">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> SCP is an Extradimensional space (hereafter referred to as ES). ES exists as a parallel dimension to our own. ES is filled with esoteric machines that continuously enforce the physical logical and thaumaturgic laws of reality.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> foundation discovers common abstract mechanism enabling magic. Through prodding it manage to open a door to ES. Finds machines and fucks with them discovering that they sustain the laws of the universe. ES has a layered structure and foundation goes deeper uncovering larger machines responsible for more significant laws. Security is tight and progress becomes harder as they get further in. As the foundation make progress, they learn that our universe is built of the foundation of one that came before. Nothing about this prior universe will ever make sense to us because it does not use any of the laws we use. The old universe ended because of a great machine that destroyed it while building another. The first great reveal is that said machine is the SCP.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The foundation find that some of the machines seem to have no effect on enforcing universal laws. A brave researcher fucks with one without permission and causes it to output a huge mass of metal. Analysis of this metal reveals some haphazard data encoded within. Foundation works out that the machine is trying to deliver a message. estimates that as much as 70% of the machine is dedicated to nothing more than composing and outputting a message. They integrate mechanical typewriters into parts of the machine and try and teach it English. After a very long time they get something coherent. The message simply reads.</p>
<p>“this is our gift to you.”</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Every law we know of both physical, logical and thaumaturgical is not innate and is instead enforced upon reality by a machine that you can physically touch. Where did the machines come from and what would happen if they were switched off?</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>
<p>I’m not 100% sure about all of the narrative beats here but this is the fundamental idea that I want to write. There are some fun bits that could be thrown in like logs from the foundation testing on the machines. More about the machine’s relationship with the forces of thaumaturgy could be explored.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

