			<div class="content" id="post-content-4831472">
									

<p>Hi Thanks for the feedback. You asked some questions directly so I'm going to answer them here.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Is this a 'mechanism' as in like, a physical machine? or a mechanism as in an abstract process?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It's an abstract process. Because the whole environment of the universe is a product of this machine on both a physical and metaphysical level the machine can leave abstract triggers that allow you to interface with it. If you know anything about computers it's a little like an OS providing code running under it with access to system calls that can be used to request more memory and print stuff to the screen. Its like a system call embedded in reality on an abstract level.</p>
<p>You would use these triggers with your mind but it would be very difficult. Something only a few people can do. I'll leave the actual experience of using one of these triggers mostly up to the imagination but indicate that it's something fundamentally difficult to express in words (hence why it's such a hard skill to teach).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>What's the security like here? How does it make progress harder?</p>
<p>This feels…like a really weird way to solve this problem</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I agree. This was little bit of a throwaway line.</p>
<p>In my head I imagined big doors with complicated mechanical locks that take weeks to crack. Shifting hallways and an impossible to map structure. This is a tad generic though so I will probably try and develop this before my next idea draft.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Regarding the narrative being passive I'd say I agree with that. I'm going to go away and think about all of this before coming back and rewriting this document. I'm very confident that I can polish this up.</p>
<p>Your feedback has been indispensable and I hope you will take another look when the next version is ready.</p>
<p>Thanks for your time.</p>

							</div>

								
